# Chess Mate-in-1 Practice App

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
    <title>Chess Mate-in-1 Practice</title>
    <style>
        * {
            margin: 0;
            padding: 0;
            box-sizing: border-box;
        }

        body {
            font-family: 'Segoe UI', Tahoma, Geneva, Verdana, sans-serif;
            background: linear-gradient(135deg, #1a1a2e 0%, #16213e 100%);
            min-height: 100vh;
            display: flex;
            flex-direction: column;
            align-items: center;
            padding: 20px;
            color: #fff;
        }

        h1 {
            margin-bottom: 10px;
            font-size: 2rem;
            text-shadow: 2px 2px 4px rgba(0,0,0,0.5);
        }

        .subtitle {
            color: #8892b0;
            margin-bottom: 20px;
        }

        .scenario-selector {
            display: flex;
            gap: 10px;
            margin-bottom: 20px;
            flex-wrap: wrap;
            justify-content: center;
        }

        .scenario-btn {
            padding: 12px 24px;
            font-size: 1rem;
            border: 2px solid #4a5568;
            background: #2d3748;
            color: #fff;
            border-radius: 8px;
            cursor: pointer;
            transition: all 0.3s ease;
        }

        .scenario-btn:hover {
            background: #4a5568;
            transform: translateY(-2px);
        }

        .scenario-btn.active {
            background: #3182ce;
            border-color: #63b3ed;
            box-shadow: 0 0 15px rgba(49, 130, 206, 0.5);
        }

        .game-container {
            display: flex;
            flex-direction: column;
            align-items: center;
            gap: 20px;
        }

        .scenario-info {
            background: #2d3748;
            padding: 15px 25px;
            border-radius: 10px;
            text-align: center;
            max-width: 500px;
        }

        .scenario-title {
            font-size: 1.3rem;
            color: #63b3ed;
            margin-bottom: 5px;
        }

        .scenario-desc {
            color: #a0aec0;
        }

        .board-container {
            position: relative;
        }

        .board {
            display: grid;
            grid-template-columns: repeat(8, 70px);
            grid-template-rows: repeat(8, 70px);
            border: 4px solid #4a5568;
            border-radius: 4px;
            box-shadow: 0 10px 40px rgba(0,0,0,0.5);
        }

        .square {
            width: 70px;
            height: 70px;
            display: flex;
            justify-content: center;
            align-items: center;
            font-size: 50px;
            cursor: pointer;
            position: relative;
            transition: background-color 0.2s;
        }

        .square.light {
            background-color: #f0d9b5;
        }

        .square.dark {
            background-color: #b58863;
        }

        .square.highlight {
            box-shadow: inset 0 0 0 4px rgba(255, 255, 0, 0.7);
        }

        .square.valid-move {
            background-color: rgba(0, 255, 0, 0.3) !important;
        }

        .square.selected {
            box-shadow: inset 0 0 0 4px rgba(0, 150, 255, 0.8);
        }

        .square.last-move {
            box-shadow: inset 0 0 0 4px rgba(255, 200, 0, 0.6);
        }

        .piece {
            cursor: grab;
            user-select: none;
            transition: transform 0.1s;
            text-shadow: 2px 2px 2px rgba(0,0,0,0.3);
        }

        .piece:active {
            cursor: grabbing;
        }

        .piece.dragging {
            opacity: 0.5;
        }

        .piece.white {
            filter: drop-shadow(1px 1px 1px rgba(0,0,0,0.5));
        }

        .piece.black {
            filter: drop-shadow(1px 1px 1px rgba(0,0,0,0.5));
        }

        .coordinates {
            position: absolute;
            font-size: 12px;
            font-weight: bold;
            pointer-events: none;
        }

        .file-coord {
            bottom: 2px;
            right: 4px;
        }

        .rank-coord {
            top: 2px;
            left: 4px;
        }

        .square.light .coordinates {
            color: #b58863;
        }

        .square.dark .coordinates {
            color: #f0d9b5;
        }

        .controls {
            display: flex;
            gap: 15px;
            margin-top: 10px;
        }

        .btn {
            padding: 12px 30px;
            font-size: 1rem;
            border: none;
            border-radius: 8px;
            cursor: pointer;
            transition: all 0.3s ease;
            font-weight: 600;
        }

        .btn-reset {
            background: #e53e3e;
            color: white;
        }

        .btn-reset:hover {
            background: #c53030;
            transform: translateY(-2px);
        }

        .btn-hint {
            background: #805ad5;
            color: white;
        }

        .btn-hint:hover {
            background: #6b46c1;
            transform: translateY(-2px);
        }

        .feedback {
            margin-top: 15px;
            padding: 20px 40px;
            border-radius: 10px;
            font-size: 1.3rem;
            font-weight: bold;
            text-align: center;
            opacity: 0;
            transform: scale(0.8);
            transition: all 0.4s ease;
        }

        .feedback.show {
            opacity: 1;
            transform: scale(1);
        }

        .feedback.success {
            background: linear-gradient(135deg, #48bb78 0%, #38a169 100%);
            color: white;
            box-shadow: 0 5px 20px rgba(72, 187, 120, 0.5);
        }

        .feedback.error {
            background: linear-gradient(135deg, #fc8181 0%, #e53e3e 100%);
            color: white;
            box-shadow: 0 5px 20px rgba(229, 62, 62, 0.5);
        }

        .feedback.hint {
            background: linear-gradient(135deg, #805ad5 0%, #6b46c1 100%);
            color: white;
            box-shadow: 0 5px 20px rgba(128, 90, 213, 0.5);
        }

        .checkmate-overlay {
            position: absolute;
            top: 0;
            left: 0;
            right: 0;
            bottom: 0;
            background: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.7);
            display: flex;
            justify-content: center;
            align-items: center;
            opacity: 0;
            pointer-events: none;
            transition: opacity 0.5s;
            border-radius: 4px;
        }

        .checkmate-overlay.show {
            opacity: 1;
            pointer-events: auto;
        }

        .checkmate-text {
            font-size: 3rem;
            font-weight: bold;
            color: #ffd700;
            text-shadow: 0 0 20px rgba(255, 215, 0, 0.8);
            animation: pulse 1s ease-in-out infinite;
        }

        @keyframes pulse {
            0%, 100% { transform: scale(1); }
            50% { transform: scale(1.1); }
        }

        .move-count {
            color: #a0aec0;
            font-size: 0.9rem;
        }

        .dragging-piece {
            position: fixed;
            pointer-events: none;
            z-index: 1000;
            font-size: 60px;
            transform: translate(-50%, -50%);
            text-shadow: 3px 3px 5px rgba(0,0,0,0.5);
        }
    </style>
</head>
<body>
    <h1>♔ Mate in 1 Practice ♚</h1>
    <p class="subtitle">White to move - Find the checkmate!</p>

    <div class="scenario-selector">
        <button class="scenario-btn active" data-scenario="0">Back Rank Mate</button>
        <button class="scenario-btn" data-scenario="1">Ladder Mate</button>
        <button class="scenario-btn" data-scenario="2">Queen & King Mate</button>
    </div>

    <div class="game-container">
        <div class="scenario-info">
            <div class="scenario-title" id="scenarioTitle">Back Rank Mate</div>
            <div class="scenario-desc" id="scenarioDesc">Use your rook to deliver checkmate on the back rank!</div>
        </div>

        <div class="board-container">
            <div class="board" id="board"></div>
            <div class="checkmate-overlay" id="checkmateOverlay">
                <div class="checkmate-text">✓ CHECKMATE!</div>
            </div>
        </div>

        <div class="controls">
            <button class="btn btn-reset" id="resetBtn">↺ Reset Position</button>
            <button class="btn btn-hint" id="hintBtn">💡 Show Hint</button>
        </div>

        <div class="feedback" id="feedback"></div>
        <div class="move-count" id="moveCount">Attempts: 0</div>
    </div>

    <script>
        // Chess piece unicode characters
        const PIECES = {
            K: '♔', Q: '♕', R: '♖', B: '♗', N: '♘', P: '♙',
            k: '♚', q: '♛', r: '♜', b: '♝', n: '♞', p: '♟'
        };

        // Scenario definitions
        const scenarios = [
            {
                name: "Back Rank Mate",
                description: "Use your rook to deliver checkmate on the back rank!",
                // Board state: piece positions
                board: {
                    'd2': 'K', 'e1': 'R',  // White pieces
                    'a8': 'k', 'a7': 'p', 'b7': 'p'  // Black pieces
                },
                solution: { from: 'e1', to: 'e8' },
                hint: "The black king is trapped by its own pawns..."
            },
            {
                name: "Ladder Mate",
                description: "Use your rooks to deliver a classic ladder mate!",
                board: {
                    'a1': 'K', 'g7': 'R', 'b6': 'R',  // White pieces
                    'h8': 'k'  // Black pieces
                },
                solution: { from: 'b6', to: 'b8' },
                hint: "One rook cuts off the escape, the other delivers mate..."
            },
            {
                name: "Queen & King Mate",
                description: "Use your queen supported by the king to deliver checkmate!",
                board: {
                    'g6': 'K', 'f4': 'Q',  // White pieces
                    'h8': 'k', 'h7': 'p'  // Black pieces
                },
                solution: { from: 'f4', to: 'f8' },
                hint: "The king supports the queen from a distance..."
            }
        ];

        // Game state
        let currentScenario = 0;
        let boardState = {};
        let selectedSquare = null;
        let attempts = 0;
        let solved = false;
        let draggedPiece = null;
        let draggedFrom = null;
        let dragElement = null;

        // DOM elements
        const boardEl = document.getElementById('board');
        const feedbackEl = document.getElementById('feedback');
        const moveCountEl = document.getElementById('moveCount');
        const checkmateOverlay = document.getElementById('checkmateOverlay');
        const scenarioTitle = document.getElementById('scenarioTitle');
        const scenarioDesc = document.getElementById('scenarioDesc');

        // Initialize the board
        function createBoard() {
            boardEl.innerHTML = '';
            const files = ['a', 'b', 'c', 'd', 'e', 'f', 'g', 'h'];

            for (let rank = 8; rank >= 1; rank--) {
                for (let fileIndex = 0; fileIndex < 8; fileIndex++) {
                    const file = files[fileIndex];
                    const square = document.createElement('div');
                    const squareId = file + rank;

                    square.className = 'square ' + ((rank + fileIndex) % 2 === 0 ? 'dark' : 'light');
                    square.dataset.square = squareId;

                    // Add coordinates
                    if (fileIndex === 0) {
                        const rankCoord = document.createElement('span');
                        rankCoord.className = 'coordinates rank-coord';
                        rankCoord.textContent = rank;
                        square.appendChild(rankCoord);
                    }
                    if (rank === 1) {
                        const fileCoord = document.createElement('span');
                        fileCoord.className = 'coordinates file-coord';
                        fileCoord.textContent = file;
                        square.appendChild(fileCoord);
                    }

                    square.addEventListener('click', () => handleSquareClick(squareId));
                    square.addEventListener('dragover', handleDragOver);
                    square.addEventListener('drop', (e) => handleDrop(e, squareId));

                    boardEl.appendChild(square);
                }
            }
        }

        // Load a scenario
        function loadScenario(index) {
            currentScenario = index;
            const scenario = scenarios[index];

            // Update UI
            scenarioTitle.textContent = scenario.name;
            scenarioDesc.textContent = scenario.description;

            // Update button states
            document.querySelectorAll('.scenario-btn').forEach((btn, i) => {
                btn.classList.toggle('active', i === index);
            });

            // Reset game state
            boardState = { ...scenario.board };
            selectedSquare = null;
            attempts = 0;
            solved = false;

            // Update display
            updateBoard();
            hideFeedback();
            hideCheckmate();
            updateMoveCount();
        }

        // Update the board display
        function updateBoard() {
            document.querySelectorAll('.square').forEach(square => {
                const squareId = square.dataset.square;

                // Remove existing piece
                const existingPiece = square.querySelector('.piece');
                if (existingPiece) {
                    existingPiece.remove();
                }

                // Add piece if present
                const piece = boardState[squareId];
                if (piece) {
                    const pieceEl = document.createElement('span');
                    pieceEl.className = 'piece ' + (piece === piece.toUpperCase() ? 'white' : 'black');
                    pieceEl.textContent = PIECES[piece];
                    pieceEl.draggable = piece === piece.toUpperCase() && !solved;

                    pieceEl.addEventListener('dragstart', (e) => handleDragStart(e, squareId, piece));
                    pieceEl.addEventListener('dragend', handleDragEnd);

                    square.appendChild(pieceEl);
                }

                // Clear highlights
                square.classList.remove('selected', 'valid-move', 'last-move');
            });
        }

        // Handle drag start
        function handleDragStart(e, squareId, piece) {
            if (solved) {
                e.preventDefault();
                return;
            }

            draggedPiece = piece;
            draggedFrom = squareId;

            // Create floating piece element
            dragElement = document.createElement('div');
            dragElement.className = 'dragging-piece';
            dragElement.textContent = PIECES[piece];
            document.body.appendChild(dragElement);

            // Set drag image to transparent
            const transparent = document.createElement('canvas');
            transparent.width = 1;
            transparent.height = 1;
            e.dataTransfer.setDragImage(transparent, 0, 0);

            // Update position on mouse move
            document.addEventListener('mousemove', updateDragPosition);
            document.addEventListener('drag', updateDragPosition);

            e.target.classList.add('dragging');
            highlightValidMoves(squareId);
        }

        function updateDragPosition(e) {
            if (dragElement) {
                dragElement.style.left = e.clientX + 'px';
                dragElement.style.top = e.clientY + 'px';
            }
        }

        // Handle drag over
        function handleDragOver(e) {
            e.preventDefault();
        }

        // Handle drag end
        function handleDragEnd(e) {
            if (dragElement) {
                dragElement.remove();
                dragElement = null;
            }
            document.removeEventListener('mousemove', updateDragPosition);
            document.removeEventListener('drag', updateDragPosition);

            document.querySelectorAll('.piece').forEach(p => p.classList.remove('dragging'));
            clearHighlights();
            draggedPiece = null;
            draggedFrom = null;
        }

        // Handle drop
        function handleDrop(e, targetSquare) {
            e.preventDefault();

            if (draggedFrom && draggedPiece && !solved) {
                attemptMove(draggedFrom, targetSquare);
            }

            handleDragEnd(e);
        }

        // Handle square click
        function handleSquareClick(squareId) {
            if (solved) return;

            const piece = boardState[squareId];

            if (selectedSquare) {
                // Try to make a move
                if (squareId !== selectedSquare) {
                    attemptMove(selectedSquare, squareId);
                }
                selectedSquare = null;
                clearHighlights();
            } else if (piece && piece === piece.toUpperCase()) {
                // Select white piece
                selectedSquare = squareId;
                highlightSquare(squareId, 'selected');
                highlightValidMoves(squareId);
            }
        }

        // Highlight valid move squares (simplified - just visual)
        function highlightValidMoves(fromSquare) {
            const piece = boardState[fromSquare];
            if (!piece) return;

            const moves = getValidMoves(fromSquare, piece);
            moves.forEach(square => {
                highlightSquare(square, 'valid-move');
            });
        }

        // Get valid moves for a piece (simplified)
        function getValidMoves(from, piece) {
            const moves = [];
            const [fromFile, fromRank] = [from.charCodeAt(0) - 97, parseInt(from[1])];
            const pieceType = piece.toUpperCase();

            for (let file = 0; file < 8; file++) {
                for (let rank = 1; rank <= 8; rank++) {
                    const to = String.fromCharCode(97 + file) + rank;
                    if (to === from) continue;

                    // Don't capture own pieces
                    const targetPiece = boardState[to];
                    if (targetPiece && (piece === piece.toUpperCase()) === (targetPiece === targetPiece.toUpperCase())) {
                        continue;
                    }

                    if (isValidMove(from, to, pieceType)) {
                        moves.push(to);
                    }
                }
            }
            return moves;
        }

        // Check if a move is valid (simplified chess rules)
        function isValidMove(from, to, pieceType) {
            const [fromFile, fromRank] = [from.charCodeAt(0) - 97, parseInt(from[1])];
            const [toFile, toRank] = [to.charCodeAt(0) - 97, parseInt(to[1])];
            const fileDiff = Math.abs(toFile - fromFile);
            const rankDiff = Math.abs(toRank - fromRank);

            switch (pieceType) {
                case 'K':
                    return fileDiff <= 1 && rankDiff <= 1;
                case 'Q':
                    return (fileDiff === 0 || rankDiff === 0 || fileDiff === rankDiff) && 
                           !isBlocked(from, to);
                case 'R':
                    return (fileDiff === 0 || rankDiff === 0) && !isBlocked(from, to);
                case 'B':
                    return fileDiff === rankDiff && !isBlocked(from, to);
                case 'N':
                    return (fileDiff === 2 && rankDiff === 1) || (fileDiff === 1 && rankDiff === 2);
                case 'P':
                    const direction = 1; // White pawns move up
                    if (fileDiff === 0 && toRank - fromRank === direction && !boardState[to]) {
                        return true;
                    }
                    if (fileDiff === 1 && toRank - fromRank === direction && boardState[to]) {
                        return true;
                    }
                    return false;
                default:
                    return false;
            }
        }

        // Check if path is blocked (for sliding pieces)
        function isBlocked(from, to) {
            const [fromFile, fromRank] = [from.charCodeAt(0) - 97, parseInt(from[1])];
            const [toFile, toRank] = [to.charCodeAt(0) - 97, parseInt(to[1])];

            const fileStep = Math.sign(toFile - fromFile);
            const rankStep = Math.sign(toRank - fromRank);

            let currentFile = fromFile + fileStep;
            let currentRank = fromRank + rankStep;

            while (currentFile !== toFile || currentRank !== toRank) {
                const square = String.fromCharCode(97 + currentFile) + currentRank;
                if (boardState[square]) return true;
                currentFile += fileStep;
                currentRank += rankStep;
            }

            return false;
        }

        // Attempt a move
        function attemptMove(from, to) {
            const piece = boardState[from];
            if (!piece || piece !== piece.toUpperCase()) return; // Only white can move

            const pieceType = piece.toUpperCase();

            // Check if move is valid
            if (!isValidMove(from, to, pieceType)) {
                showFeedback("Invalid move!", "error");
                return;
            }

            // Don't capture own pieces
            const targetPiece = boardState[to];
            if (targetPiece && targetPiece === targetPiece.toUpperCase()) {
                showFeedback("Can't capture your own piece!", "error");
                return;
            }

            attempts++;
            updateMoveCount();

            const scenario = scenarios[currentScenario];

            // Check if this is the correct solution
            if (from === scenario.solution.from && to === scenario.solution.to) {
                // Make the move
                delete boardState[from];
                boardState[to] = piece;
                updateBoard();

                // Show last move highlight
                highlightSquare(from, 'last-move');
                highlightSquare(to, 'last-move');

                // Success!
                solved = true;
                setTimeout(() => {
                    showCheckmate();
                    showFeedback("🎉 Brilliant! Checkmate in " + attempts + " attempt" + (attempts > 1 ? "s" : "") + "!", "success");
                }, 200);
            } else {
                // Wrong move
                showFeedback("Not checkmate! Try again.", "error");
            }
        }

        // Highlight a square
        function highlightSquare(squareId, className) {
            const square = document.querySelector(`[data-square="${squareId}"]`);
            if (square) {
                square.classList.add(className);
            }
        }

        // Clear all highlights
        function clearHighlights() {
            document.querySelectorAll('.square').forEach(square => {
                square.classList.remove('selected', 'valid-move');
            });
        }

        // Show feedback message
        function showFeedback(message, type) {
            feedbackEl.textContent = message;
            feedbackEl.className = 'feedback ' + type + ' show';

            if (type === 'error' || type === 'hint') {
                setTimeout(hideFeedback, 3000);
            }
        }

        // Hide feedback
        function hideFeedback() {
            feedbackEl.classList.remove('show');
        }

        // Show checkmate overlay
        function showCheckmate() {
            checkmateOverlay.classList.add('show');
        }

        // Hide checkmate overlay
        function hideCheckmate() {
            checkmateOverlay.classList.remove('show');
        }

        // Update move count display
        function updateMoveCount() {
            moveCountEl.textContent = `Attempts: ${attempts}`;
        }

        // Show hint
        function showHint() {
            if (!solved) {
                const scenario = scenarios[currentScenario];
                showFeedback("💡 Hint: " + scenario.hint, "hint");
            }
        }

        // Event listeners
        document.querySelectorAll('.scenario-btn').forEach(btn => {
            btn.addEventListener('click', () => {
                loadScenario(parseInt(btn.dataset.scenario));
            });
        });

        document.getElementById('resetBtn').addEventListener('click', () => {
            loadScenario(currentScenario);
        });

        document.getElementById('hintBtn').addEventListener('click', showHint);

        // Initialize
        createBoard();
        loadScenario(0);
    </script>
</body>
</html>
```

## Features

### 🎯 Three Mate-in-1 Scenarios:

1. **Back Rank Mate** - White Rook delivers checkmate by exploiting the trapped black king behind its own pawns (Re1-e8#)

2. **Ladder Mate** - Two white rooks work together to deliver a classic "lawnmower" checkmate (Rb6-b8#)

3. **Queen & King Mate** - The queen delivers checkmate with the king cutting off escape squares (Qf4-f8#)

### 🎮 Interactive Features:

- **Drag and Drop** - Pieces can be dragged to their destination squares
- **Click to Move** - Click a piece to select it, then click the destination
- **Visual Move Hints** - Valid squares are highlighted in green when a piece is selected
- **Scenario Selection** - Three buttons to switch between puzzles instantly
- **Reset Button** - Restore the position to try again
- **Hint Button** - Get a clue if you're stuck

### 📊 Visual Feedback:

- **Success Animation** - Checkmate overlay with pulsing celebration text
- **Move Highlighting** - Last move shown with yellow highlights
- **Attempt Counter** - Track how many tries it took
- **Color-coded Messages** - Green for success, red for errors, purple for hints
- **Coordinate Labels** - Files (a-h) and ranks (1-8) displayed on the board
